   420	>    `a_i >= m + K_tot >= 2`; `1 <= b <= floor((N-2)/2)`; `m <= N - 2 - K_tot`;
   421	>    `s_l <= floor((N-2)/2)`.
   422	> 3. **Local.** `a_p + sum_i r_{i,p} W_i + K_p = N`; the letters over `p` split
   423	>    into `a_p` fixed singletons plus clusters, each `G_p`-invariant with `G_p`
   424	>    transitive on it; distinct branches at `p` carry disjoint meridians; no `G_p`
   425	>    is transitive on all `N` letters.
   426	> 4. **Kills.** `2 W_i <= N` whenever `corr = 0` on `D_i` (Gate SELF); `2 W_br <= N`
   427	>    when `b = 1` (Gate LZ-KILL); `s_l = 1` whenever `mu_l = 2` (NO-RAM-2), so no
   428	>    ramified carrier exists below `N = 10`.
   429	> 5. **Corrections.** Every correction of a `mu = 2` carrier is an ordinary
   430	>    `(nu, nu+1)` cusp of the image with `k = nu - 1`; no other germ occurs.
   431	> 6. **Monodromy.** `rho : pi_1(C^2 - D_br) ->> G <= S_N` is transitive with
   432	>    nonabelian image; `gamma_i` has cycle type `1^{a_i} prod_{l->i} mu_l^{s_l}`;
   433	>    a transposition meridian forces `G = S_N`.
   434	> 7. **Degree.** `sum_i d_i iota_i = N - 2 + 2g + Sigma_inf`, and if `G` is
   435	>    primitive then `d_min(D_i) . iota_i >= N - 1` for each branched `i`; no upper
   436	>    bound on `deg A_F` in terms of `N` exists.
   437	
   438	**Survivor shape (conjectured in the charge, proved here).** Write `Gamma` for the
   439	total cost of the *nontrivial* dicriticals (`mu >= 2`) and `T = N - 1 - Gamma >= 1`
   440	for the number of trivial ones. Then a profile survives 1-6 iff it consists of
   441	
   442	- a **core**: a multiset of `c >= 1` nontrivial dicriticals `(mu_j, s_j, k_j)` of
   443	  total cost `Gamma <= N - 2`, partitioned into `b <= c` branched components; plus
   444	- `T` trivial dicriticals distributed over the branched components and over
   445	  `u >= max(0, 2-b)` new unbranched components;
   446	
   447	subject only to `2W_i <= N` on every correction-free component, `2W_br <= N` when
   448	`b = 1`, and `s_j = 1` whenever `mu_j = 2`. **The monodromy problem depends only
   449	on the core**: trivial dicriticals contribute `1`-cycles, unbranched components
   450	have trivial meridians and are invisible to `rho`; they only consume budget,
   451	tighten (LOC), and add curves to `A_F`. Since `c <= floor((N-2)/2)` and the cost
   452	of a minimal nontrivial carrier is `2`, the number of cores grows with `N` roughly
   453	like the number of partitions of `N-2` into parts `>= 2`. **There is therefore no
   454	uniform finite survivor list**, and by NO-DEG-CAP no numeric gate can produce one:
   455	the residual is a growing but explicitly enumerable family of `PI1-S_N` questions.
   456	`[D]`
   457	
   458	At the two closed degrees the shape specialises correctly, which is the control on
   459	the whole machine: `N = 4` gives exactly one row (core `(2,1,0)`, `W = (1,2)`) —
   460	the promoted `N = 4` residual; `N = 5` gives exactly the two promoted survivors,
   461	S2 (core `(2,1,0)`, `W = (1,1,2)` or `(2,2)`) and S1 (core `(2,1,1)`, `W = (1,2)`),
   462	with P2 and P3c killed by Gate SELF/LZ-KILL. No row of the closed degrees is lost
   463	and none is added.
