   281	## 5. Why the affine computation suffices
   282	
   283	The projection `pr|_D : D -> C`, `(x,y) |-> x`, is proper of degree 9:
   284	`deg_y F = 9` and `lc_y(F)` is a unit of `QQ`. A generic fibre meets `D`
   285	in nine points; `pi_1` of the complement of those nine points in the
   286	fibre is `F_9`. The discriminant `Delta subset C` is finite, of
   287	cardinality 9 (square-free support of `disc_y F`). A geometric basis of
   288	`pi_1(C \ Delta, p1)` therefore presents all finite monodromy.
   289	
   290	The loop around a large circle in the `x`-plane is the product of that
   291	geometric basis (B4). Its braid is `rho_inf`. In the ZvK presentation of
   292	the **affine** complement this loop does not add a generator or a
   293	relation beyond the product of the local relations: it *is* that
   294	product. The extra relation `xi_9 ... xi_1 = 1` is the relation at
   295	infinity in `P^2`, and presents `pi_1(P^2 - Dbar)`, which is the wrong
   296	group for `phi : pi_1(C^2 - D) -> S_4`. This is Oka's Remark 3 as used
   297	in PI1-S4-DECISION §2 (the cuspidal-cubic witness that the projective
   298	relation kills a generator the affine group retains). Affine ZvK is
