   376	## 6. Per-ideal faithfulness verdicts and exact corrections
   377	
   378	All six ideals are **UNFAITHFUL** to their advertised exhaustive meaning.
   379	For A/B the error admits false positives; for 96A/96B it cuts to a strict
   380	slice and admits false negatives; C/D inherit the A/B construction before
   381	their computations finish.  The exact replacements are specified in 7.1.
   382	
   383	| job | typed audit finding |
   384	|---|---|
   385	| `type86_A` | **UNFAITHFUL, witnessed false positive.** The charged point passes every raw generator/open but has `Delta=(8,6,19)`. |
   386	| `type86_B` | **UNFAITHFUL.** Its raw equations make the same unreduced substitution; the charged sliced points' `delta_inf=6` are consistent with the same actual `c=19`, not target `c=9`. |
   387	| `type86_C` | **UNFAITHFUL before computation.** The exact characteristic-base counterpoint in Section 4 passes old C but has a nonzero corrected degree-17 residual; replace the raw equations and add degree 10. |
   388	| `type86_D` | **UNFAITHFUL before computation.** The Section 4 characteristic-base point passes old D but has corrected `g_15!=0`; the raw list also omits gap residuals at 10 and 4. |
   389	| `type96_A` | **UNFAITHFUL strict slice.** EMPTY kills only the slice `a15=a12=a9=a6=0`, not the full type. |
   390	| `type96_B` | **UNFAITHFUL strict slice.** The same; in fact an exact four-node realization exists below. |
   391	
   392	Two supplementary formulas already on disk give useful exact negative
   393	controls for the old `(9,6)` EMPTY interpretation.  They are reproduced here
   394	so the conclusion does not depend on a label in those reports.
   395	
   396	For `(9,6,4)`, put
   397	
   398	```text
   399	p=t^9+3t^7+21/4*t^5+35/8*t^3+63/32*t,
   400	q0=t^6+2t^4+5/2*t^2,                  y=q0+3/4.
   401	```
   402	
   403	The identity recorded and coefficient-checkable at
   404	`xmodel/hf-twin-964-grok46-20260831.md:109-133` is
   405	
   406	```text
   407	y^3-p^2=27/1024*(8t^4+13t^2+16).
   408	```
   409	
   410	Hence, in the **shared constant-zero chart**,
   411	
   412	```text
   413	p^2-q0^3-(9/4)q0^2-(27/16)q0-27/64
   414	  =-27/1024*(8t^4+13t^2+16).
   415	```
   416	
   417	This is a proper corrected-locus point of exact degree 4, while raw
   418	`p^2-q0^3` has degree 12.  It also passes the affine-immersion open.  With
   419	`z=t^2`,
   420	
   421	```text
   422	q0'=t*(6z^2+8z+5),
   423	p' mod (6z^2+8z+5)=-27z/8-117/32.
   424	```
   425	
   426	The latter can vanish only at `z=-13/12`, where the quadratic has value
   427	`27/8`, and `p'(0)=63/32`; hence `p',q0'` have no common root.  Exact
   428	degree 4 together with `gcd(9,6,4)=1` also rules out a common right
   429	component.  Thus the full corrected open is already NONEMPTY.
   430	The cited desk analysis proves four nodes and leaves affine delta two as
   431	either two more nodes or one `A_3` (`ibid.:135-157`), so it does not by
   432	itself settle the six-node realization question.
   433	
   434	For `(9,6,2)`, put
   435	
   436	```text
   437	q=t^6+8t^2,                 p=t^9+12t^5+24t,
   438	p^2-q^3-64q=64t^2.
   439	```
   440	
   441	This lies in the shared chart and is proper: the identity recovers `t^2`,
   442	then `t=p/(t^8+12t^4+24)`.  Its infinity type is therefore
   443	`Delta=(9,6,2)`, `beta_1=25`, `delta_inf=24`, so `delta_aff=28-24=4`.
   444	Let `w=t^4`.  Each of the two nonzero simple roots of
   445	`w^2+12w+24` yields two pairs `{t,-t}`, one for each sign of `t^2`.
   446	Within a fixed `w` those two pair-images have opposite nonzero
   447	`q=t^2(w+8)`, while
   448	`q^2=w*(w+8)^2=-8*(w+12)` distinguishes the two `w`-families.  Thus all
   449	four images are distinct.  At them
   450	
   451	```text
   452	p'=8w(w+6) != 0,             q'=2t(3w+8) != 0,
   453	```
   454	
   455	and the velocities at `t,-t` have nonzero determinant.  They are four
   456	ordinary nodes.  Since they exhaust `delta_aff=4`, there are no omitted
   457	singularities.  This independently recovers the pair calculation in
   458	`xmodel/block-descent-a1-genus-four-cable-b1-hostile-review-grok46-20260831.md:245-267`.
   459	Thus `type96_B` is not merely NONEMPTY after correction: its advertised
   460	nodal type is **REALIZED**.
