+## 6. Strongest counterexample attack
+
+### New exact result: the displayed `(9,6,4)` curve is six-nodal
+
+For the banked parametrization `[HF:109-148]`, set `u=s+t`, `v=st` and take the
+two divided differences `A=(x(s)-x(t))/(s-t)`,
+`B=(y(s)-y(t))/(s-t)`. Exact arithmetic over `QQ` gives
+
+```text
+B = u(2u^4-8u^2v+4u^2+6v^2-8v+5)/2,
+u(8v+11)=0,       u(8u^2+35)=0              modulo (A,B).
+```
+
+The `u=0` branch is the already banked squarefree quartic producing four
+nodes. On `u!=0`, `v=-11/8` and `u^2=-35/8`, hence exactly two further unordered
+pairs. Their pair discriminant is `9/8`; their common images are
+`y=21/512`, `x=-297u/4096`, so they are distinct from each other and from the
+`x=0` nodes. The velocity determinant divided by `s-t` reduces to `315/8`, so
+both are transverse. Since the parametrization is immersive and its exact
+affine delta is six `[HF:131-148]`, these six ordinary nodes exhaust all affine
+singularities.
+
