+nodes. On `u!=0`, `v=-11/8` and `u^2=-35/8`, hence exactly two further unordered
+pairs; direct substitution makes `A=B=0`, and the `v`-eliminant has only this
+linear factor besides the `u=0` quartic. Their pair discriminant is `9/8`; their common images are
+`y=21/512`, `x=-297u/4096`, so they are distinct from each other and from the
+`x=0` nodes. The velocity determinant divided by `s-t` reduces to `315/8`, so
+both are transverse. Since the parametrization is immersive and its exact
+affine delta is six `[HF:131-148]`, these six ordinary nodes exhaust all affine
+singularities.
